Limit: only mentions the daemon's own subscriber delivers are floored: an envelope with no signed time, which is every one the local socket parses, is not compared with the binding's creation
Limit: rows admitted before this change are not recognised, because an owner's payload keeps no signed time; the three OWNER_MESSAGE rows admitted live on 2026-10-03 from 2026-08-09 mentions stay PENDING until the Logic Pro MCP PRIMARY_CTO claims each and rejects it with role_owner_message_reject
Limit: the floor is whole seconds, as created_at is, so an event signed in the fraction of the binding's start second before the binding is admitted
Warn: BUZZ_MENTION_PRECEDES_BINDING is the one refusal that moves the subscriber's window, and that is safe only because a binding's creation is never later than now and a later generation's is later; a code added to that mapping without both properties lets a refusal choose the window
Warn: a new binding generation raises the floor, so a mention signed before a takeover is refused even when it was sent while the role was between holders and retried
